Think of updating a variable like putting a new toy into your existing box. You don't need a new box (`let`), you just put the new thing inside using the `=` sign.

Here is how you can fill in the missing pieces:

```javascript
let currentLevel = 1;
console.log(currentLevel); // This prints 1

// Hint 1: Change the value like this:
currentLevel = 5;

// Hint 2: Print it again using console.log() just like the first one!
console.log(currentLevel);
```

